--- body ---

## Context

Reported from arena ticket 1111 (Q3 re-smoke, 2026-11-01, runs-q3-resmoke-20261101/0338-f1b).
The parent Pi ran at `--thinking xhigh` (94 turns xhigh); its one subagent child
(`code-reviewer`, 16 calls) ran at `medium`, Pi's `defaultThinkingLevel`. The subagent
extension builds the child's argv and passes no thinking level, so a delegated reviewer
silently runs at a lower effort than its parent. The author ruled (2026-11-01) that this
belongs to the harness; arena only records the child's level.

## Exit criteria

- [x] A Pi subagent child inherits the parent's thinking level unless its agent definition sets one
- [x] A test shows the child argv carries the level
